      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "James Mason, who arrived in Colorado at age 14 in 1863, later settled along Buckhorn Creek raising cattle and shaping the town’s early economy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.northerncoloradohistory.com/the-masons-of-masonville/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In its first year, Mason planted a sizable apple orchard on the Buckhorn property, marking the town’s early agricultural roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.northerncoloradohistory.com/the-masons-of-masonville/",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s post office, established in the late 19th century, became a vital hub for surrounding ranchers and travelers.",
